A||||7||hutch84fierose||GREAT CHEAP PROJECTS??????||||1||
Z||000000||hutch84fierose||07-04-2001||05:54 PM||||HEY EVERY ONE I AM 18 AND JUST GOT A FIERO I NEED SOME THINGS TO DO TO IT SO IT WILL LOOK BETTER IT IS AN 84 WHAT ARE SOME PROJECTS THAT I CAN DO WITHOUT SPEND TONNES OF MONEY THANKS FOR THE HELP JON||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierochic88||07-04-2001||05:58 PM||||Buy some black spray paint (Acrylic Engine Enamel in Universal Black).  Paint the trim and the rocker panels and mirrors as well as the sail panel supports.  <P>Clean the car and wax it.<P>Buy some sail panels from Paul McKibben (around $30 each).<P>Clean the interior and the carpets.  Buy some  seat covers if needed. <P>Clean the engine and touch up all removable engine parts with paint.<P>Good Luck!<P>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||skitime||07-04-2001||06:17 PM||||Hey Jennifer what you doing here on the 4th. <BR>You should be out having fun.  <P>Hutch you can also redo the headliner and Jennifer has a lot of experience doing that after two cars.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Urchin||07-04-2001||06:21 PM||||Everything Fierochic said is good, especially painting the trim.  That makes a big difference.  you could also paint the wheel wells (rocker guard or whatever), touch up any stone chips you may have, or if the chips are real bad on the nose (like mine is) then throw a bra on it until you can paint it.  You can also pick up some decent parts from the weckers around here if need be, ex, taillights, marker lights, interior pieces etc.<BR>Have fun<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||07-04-2001||10:25 PM||||And last but not least, you can quit yelling. (typing in all caps)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  A couple rattle cans of the right paint and you could repaint your interior, too.  If you run out of money, just drive your Fiero and enjoy!!<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000005||qwikgta||07-04-2001||11:55 PM||||Hutch...  One thing I like to do is to go to the junkyards and look for other GM stuff that will fit my fiero.  Things that were not offered in 84 or not on fieros.  Most are cheap like power rearview mirror off a fullsize GM (bonnie, 88 ect) rims, spoilers and scoops for hood ect...  If you have a stick you can make your own shortshifter by cutting and welding yours, i did and saved $35-50 that it would cost to buy one.  Engine area is easy to do cheap, (more or less) anything that can be taken off can be painted.  I also grabbed a 2.5L valve cover off a 89-90 duke and it has a cool screw on oil fill.  I painted it aluminum and will be putting it on this weekend.  Take and polish all your aluminum stuff and hit it with a clear coat to keep it freash.  Maybe mix and match your interior parts, like get black carpet and lower door panels and paint some other parts to give the interor a two tone color, (not sure if you have gray or brown).   Most of all have fun and be safe.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||KissMySSFiero||07-05-2001||11:43 AM||||Cheap stuff to do.  hehe im good at bein cheap.  if your carpet is soiled,  go the the wrecker and get some decent stuff out of a donor car($10)--- repair those ugly warps in your interior-get some super glue and acceleratior(go to a hobby shop)  remove the panels that are bad,  and go slow.  if you want to know more on that email me--($7 for glue and Accelerator,  $3bucks for acetone to get glue off fingertips)----newer steering wheel. gm is known for using parts that interchange with many of there car models.  you can get a steering wheel of many other gm cars and put it on yours.  junk yards usually sell them fairly cheap($5-$30) or you can get one from another model fiero.  go to autozone or another parts store.  autozone has a loan a tool program(buy the tool and take it back)  you can get a steering wheel puller for $15 and then return it and get all of your money back. if you have an 84 then you can change the decklid and make it look like a new model with the side vents and the smooth deck.  again a wrecking yard should have them for a not too bad price. thats all i can think of now.  the painting the trim is a good one for a low cost.  good luck<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000007||KissMySSFiero||07-05-2001||11:47 AM||||damnit...it wasnt supposed to do that(double time)------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">            <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"<p>[This message has been edited by KissMySSFiero (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||1
